Two fixtures are derived from this match, under the same licence:

- ogid_hedgehog.json: the ogid_before of every ply, as HedgeHog's reference
  implementation reads them (the "ogid_before" fields of
  github.com/kevung/ogxmparser, testdata/hedgehog-3pt-analysed.ref.json,
  which that repository's testdata/generate.py writes from ogxm_convert).
- hedgehog-3pt-analysed.cube-norm.json: the no_double_norm_eq,
  double_take_norm_eq and double_pass_norm_eq of every cube decision a
  doubler faces (each ply's analysis.cube_decision, and the analysis of a
  double ply), rounded to 1e-6, from the output of

      build/ogxm_convert --to-json < testdata/hedgehog-3pt-analysed.ogxm

  The tool is HedgeHog's reference implementation,
  gitlab.com/eranlambooij/hedgehog-public at commit
  78693ef862335ab94f80144692e3521fc1281cc7, built with `make ogxm NATIVE=0`
  and distributed under the MIT License (Copyright (c) 2026 Eran Lambooij;
  its format specifications under docs/ are CC BY 4.0). The tool's output
  is data, not a copy of its code.
